set.body:
Migrate PLSC, regularized CCA, and reduced-rank regression through secondOrder, compress, FunctionalFrame, and OperatorProgram; then delete PairedGmd as the family-specific compute engine.

Requirements:
- S_XY = secondOrder(X, L_XY, Y); complete, partial, weighted, one-to-many, and hub-factorized matching differ only in the typed row relation;
- CCA and PLS share the cross objective but use distinct typed normalization operators;
- RRR retains its directed regression coefficient map as a derived semantic object;
- existing typed regularization parameters remain explicit, but general policies/penalties are not improvised here;
- fits use the generic result contract for paired-frame symmetry, component pairing, numerical identifiability, transforms, and provenance.

Acceptance:
- PairedLatentRReferenceFixtures pass unchanged on JVM and JS;
- direct whitened cross-SVD and regression-coefficient oracles agree;
- row permutation, alignment factorization, scale, sign, and paired-subspace laws pass;
- PairedGmd and PairedGmdMetric are removed after their last family consumer migrates;
- no parallel numeric engine and no raw-double semantic API.
